#!/bin/sh
# Blocks a commit that touches docs/ while the documentation checker reports a NEW failure.
# See CLAUDE.md and docs/CLAUDE.md for the conventions it enforces.
#
# check-docs.mjs walks the whole docs/ tree rather than the staged paths, and it reads the
# WORKING TREE, not the index. Two consequences, both deliberate:
#
#   - It catches the mirror case a staged-file checker cannot: renaming a heading in A.md
#     breaks an #anchor in B.md, and a commit that stages only A.md would otherwise pass.
#   - It does NOT check exactly what is being committed. Commit with unstaged edits in docs/
#     present and the hook judged those edits, not the snapshot going in.
#
# Failures already listed in scripts/check-docs.baseline.txt are ignored, so the gate is
# "no new failures", not "no failures". Fix an entry and delete its line by hand. Never run
# `node scripts/check-docs.mjs --write-baseline` to clear a fresh failure — that silently
# converts a bug into accepted breakage, and nothing downstream can tell the difference.
#
# Conventions checking (`--conventions docs`) is not wired in yet: it still reports
# pre-existing problems, and a hook that fails on every commit gets bypassed. Add the flag
# here once that pass is clean.

git diff --cached --name-only --diff-filter=ACMR | grep -q '^docs/' || exit 0

exec node scripts/check-docs.mjs
